{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Snippet: Empty cart routes
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose:            Turn the empty cart from a dead end into a way back
                      into the range. Dawn offers one "Continue shopping"
                      link to /collections/all — a shopper who has not yet
                      chosen a door type learns nothing from that.
  Primary source:     Shopify Navigation. Reads a link list and offers its
                      top-level items (or the children of the item that has
                      them, which is where a Products → Digital Locks → …
                      menu keeps the useful routes).
  Fallback order:     children of the first parent item → top-level items →
                      render nothing (Dawn's own button still stands).
  Visibility rule:    Renders nothing when the menu is missing or empty, so
                      the empty cart is never worse than Dawn's.
  Merchant editable:  YES — entirely, by editing the menu in Navigation.
                      No parallel menu system, per the nav architecture rule.
  Dependencies:       otodor-cart.css for styling.

  Params:
    menu    link list handle (default `main-menu`)
    limit   maximum routes to show (default 4)
    title   optional heading above the routes
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign menu_handle = menu | default: 'main-menu'
  assign route_limit = limit | default: 4
  assign menu_object = linklists[menu_handle]

  # Prefer the children of the first item that has any: on this store that is
  # "Products", whose children are the categories worth offering here.
  assign routes = menu_object.links
  for link in menu_object.links
    if link.links.size > 0
      assign routes = link.links
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if routes.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="otodor-cart-empty-routes">
    {%- if title != blank -%}
      <p class="otodor-cart-empty-routes__title">{{ title | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <ul class="otodor-cart-empty-routes__list" role="list">
      {%- for link in routes limit: route_limit -%}
        <li>
          <a class="otodor-cart-empty-routes__link" href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title | escape }}</a>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
